# Production release target

- This repository has one production product target: the private shared
  MultiImageClient image-making site at
  `https://multiimageclient.alpha.fuseki.net/<private-path>/`.
- The path segment is secret and must never be printed, committed, or exposed
  in logs. An ordinary deploy must not rename DNS, TLS, the path, or nginx.
- `tpbeta` is only the colocated physical host. It is not the product/site
  identity, and its other services and vhosts are outside this repository's
  deployment scope.
- A request to **commit and push**, including the Cursor diff-tab
  commit-and-push action, is a full local+production release unless the user
  excludes a step. Order: commit the requested files; run the
  [deploy/README.md](deploy/README.md) release gate; push the requested
  branch; rebuild and restart the local `--ui` on `127.0.0.1:5960`; if that
  push updated `origin/master`, redeploy only `multiimageclient-ui.service`
  through `deploy/agent-redeploy.sh`; verify local `/healthz`, remote commit,
  fresh service start, loopback, and private vhost.
- Local restart: run `tools/restart-local-ui.sh`. Do not use
  `tools/start-ui.sh` (Surface/WSL launcher). In-flight local jobs die.
- Skip production redeploy when the push did not update `origin/master`.
  Feature-branch pushes still restart the local site.
- On this workstation, the `tpbeta` SSH alias logs in as `subcreation`, which
  does not own the checkout. Use the documented `tpbeta-root` command that
  runs the release as the `tparkour` Unix checkout owner. That account name
  does not make Terrain Parkour a deployment target. Never guess another
  checkout or service, and never replace the standard release script with an
  ad hoc host-wide update.
- Never print or disclose the site's secret path, credentials, cookies, or
  provider keys.

## Explicit additional environments

The owner authorized separate environments on this same hostname on 2026-09-08.
Use `deploy/create-environment.py` for an explicitly selected new environment.
Read `docs/workspaces-prd.md` before provisioning or updating one.
Keep the existing service, route, accounts, and data intact.
An ordinary master release still updates only `multiimageclient-ui.service`.
Additional environments require explicit target selection and independent resource budgets.

## Global administration contract (2026-09-09)

Use exactly two account levels: admin and normal. The existing ernieMultiZone account is the sole global admin.
Preserve its existing password when enabling the environment controller.
Preserve the original private route and all stored work.
Additional environments can use owner-selected public URL names; never treat the original private route as public.
Enforce membership and feature switches on API requests, not only in the frontend.
Normal members may see shared environment activity, but never raw application logs or global administration.
Install the privileged reconciler as root-owned code outside application-writable directories.
